From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:53:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(update): retain descendant identity across exit races
 [daveey]

The cancellation test passed its death assertion but could fail in finally:
a pid_exists check did not guarantee that Process(pid).kill could still
signal it. Its status poll had the same check/use race, and reconstructing
a Process after cancellation discarded PID creation-time custody.

Capture the Process at READY, before cancellation, and use its identity
for polling and cleanup. Treat only NoSuchProcess as gone; preserve
AccessDenied failures, the three-second death deadline and real tree
cancellation. Verify failure cleanup also reaches a dead/zombie state.

Proof: real owned children are killed and reaped precisely before status
and kill. Without the exception handling both fail NoSuchProcess; with it
they pass. Retained-identity mismatch leaves the real child untouched.
Disabling production killpg makes the original test fail its cancellation
assertion; a permanent mutation control verifies that failure and cleanup.

